Package: rnaseqwrapper
Title: Wrapper Functions for a Basic RNA-Seq Analysis Workflow
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Nosakhare", "Osaro", email = "osaronosakhare@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A small set of wrapper functions implementing a basic RNA-seq
    differential expression workflow: loading a gene-by-sample count
    matrix, simple library-size normalization (counts-per-million), a
    per-gene two-group differential expression test with
    Benjamini-Hochberg adjustment, and a base-graphics volcano plot. This
    is a teaching/demonstration package rather than a Bioconductor-grade
    tool: it does not model counts with a negative binomial distribution
    the way DESeq2 or edgeR do.
